GVS chatbot
===========

This project's own code has no licence chosen yet (planned: Apache-2.0).

It includes data generated from the third-party sources below
(backend/data/generated/lexicon.json, backend/evals/oos.jsonl). Each source is
pinned by sha256 in backend/data/sources.toml and rebuilt with
`uv run --group build python -m tools.build_lexicon`.

STATUS: licence review pending. Items marked [REVIEW] need a decision before
any public release; the rest only need this notice kept with the data.

- GeoNames cities15000 - city and alternate city names.
  CC BY 4.0. https://www.geonames.org  Data was filtered and reformatted.
  Obtained via the npm package cities-15000-structured 1.0.1 (MIT).

- Unicode CLDR 49 (cldr-localenames-full) - country names in en, en-IN, hi, hi-Latn.
  Copyright (c) 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc. Unicode License v3.

- i18n-iso-countries 7.14.0 - country names and alternatives in en and hi. MIT.

- [REVIEW] world-countries 5.1.0 (mledoze/countries) - alternative spellings,
  official names and demonyms. ODbL 1.0 (share-alike for the derived database).

- [REVIEW] jneidel/job-titles - job titles mapped to profession buckets. No
  licence file; compiled from sources including johnpcarty/Thesaurus-of-Job-Titles
  (GPL-3.0) and fluquid/find_job_titles (MIT).

- CLINC150 (Larson et al., 2019) - off-topic test set only, not part of the bot.
  CC BY 3.0. https://github.com/clinc/oos-eval

- wordfreq 3.1.1 (Robyn Speer) - build-time only, used to skip common English
  words and to list them for the typo guard. Code Apache-2.0; word lists
  CC BY-SA 4.0. The list of common English words is stored in the generated file.

Runtime dependencies: pydantic (MIT). Development: pytest, pytest-cov, ruff,
mypy (MIT/Apache-2.0).
